## Image GDC dense output

Image GDC corrected depth should be dense by default.

Use:

    corrected_depth = raw_depth.copy()
    corrected_depth[corrected_pixels] = corrected_values
    corrected_depth[sparse_anchor_pixels] = sparse_depth[sparse_anchor_pixels]

Do not leave non-corrected pixels as -1 unless explicitly requested.

Save stats to:

    image_gdc/stats/image_gdc_stats.csv

Include:

    output_valid_ratio
    output_valid_pixels
    anchor_reject_ratio_abs2m
    raw_anchor_mae_before_gdc
    corrected_anchor_mae_after_gdc

