6. Remove unnecessary default artifacts

Do not run these in the default Range-GDC guide evaluation pipeline:

gdc_depthmap2ptc
gdc_r64_sparsify
anchor_ptc_to_range
full preview generation

Reason:

image GDC can be evaluated by projecting corrected depth directly to range.
Range GDC anchor should be generated from GT range by row masking, not by sparse pointcloud reprojection.
preview should be optional because it is slow and creates many files.

Support them only with explicit flags:

--export-pointcloud
--make-preview
--preview-max-items 100
7. Range GDC anchor generation

Do not use:

gdc/sparsify.py -> sparse_pointcloud -> ptc-to-range

for Range GDC anchor.

Instead:

GT velodyne
-> gt_range/G64_range, shape=(64,1024)
-> make_anchor_from_gt_range
-> keep only rows [5,7,9,11]
-> zero out all other rows

Validation:

actual_rows = np.where(anchor_range > 0)[0]
assert np.array_equal(actual_rows, np.array([5,7,9,11]))

If this fails, stop the pipeline.

8. Image GDC output should be dense by default

Make image GDC corrected depth dense by default.

Desired behavior:

new_depth = raw_depth.copy()
new_depth[corrected_pixels] = corrected_values
new_depth[sparse_anchor_pixels] = sparse_depth[sparse_anchor_pixels]

Avoid sparse output like:

new_depth = np.full_like(raw_depth, -1)

unless explicitly requested.

Add config:

image_gdc:
  dense_output: true
  disable_subsample: true

The stage should save image_gdc/stats.csv with:

output_valid_ratio
output_valid_pixels
anchor_reject_ratio_abs2m
raw_anchor_mae_before_gdc
corrected_anchor_mae_after_gdc
